## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook case of **"coverage without verification"** — every production method is called (achieving line coverage) but almost nothing is actually asserted. These tests will pass even if every method returns garbage or silently corrupts data.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Missing Assertions (tests prove nothing)

**1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)** — Fire-and-forget, zero assertions.
```csharp
// BROKEN: Passes even if Save() silently drops the product
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// FIX:
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(retrieved);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);
```

**2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)** — Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the new price.
```csharp
// BROKEN: Passes even if price is unchanged or set to 0
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

// FIX:
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", updated.Name); // verify Name wasn't clobbered
```

**3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)** — Calls delete but never confirms the product is gone.
```csharp
// BROKEN: Passes even if Delete is a no-op
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

// FIX:
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)** — Captures return value into nothing, asserts nothing.
```csharp
// BROKEN: Passes if count is -1, 999, or anything
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();

// FIX:
Assert.AreEqual(0, _catalog.GetProductCount());
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

**5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)** — Applies 10% discount, never verifies any prices changed.
```csharp
// BROKEN: Passes even if discount is applied as 100% or not at all
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);

// FIX:
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);  // 9.99 * 0.9
